<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia May merchandise imports A$6.456 bln.</title>
<headline>Australia May merchandise imports A$6.456 bln.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's international merchandise imports stood at A$6.456 billion in May from a reported A$6.767 billion in April, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>This measure is compiled from information submitted by importers or their agents to the Australian Customs Service. It is not seasonally adjusted nor is it reported on the same balance-of-payments basis as the monthly balance on goods and services or quarterly current account data.  </p>
<p>  IMPORTS					  May		April</p>
<p>  Food, live animals		     A$234 million	A$241 million</p>
<p>  Beverages, tobacco			  37 million	   44 million</p>
<p>  Crude materials, except fuels	  137 million	  122 million</p>
<p>  Mineral fuels, related materials     447 million	  372 million</p>
<p>  Animal, vegetable oils, fats	    21 million	   22 million</p>
<p>  Chemical and related products	  748 million	  799 million</p>
<p>  Manufactured goods			 892 million	  951 million</p>
<p>  Machinery and transport		2,991 million	3,192 million</p>
<p>  Miscellaneous manufactures	     898 million	  975 million</p>
<p>Commodities and transactions  </p>
<p>  not classified elsewhere		52 million	   49 million</p>
<p>  Total imports			  6,456 million	6,767 million</p>
<p>-- Canberra bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
